; The lowering worklist resolves a form head local-first, exactly as the
; validator does (S7): `(bind-group (entry))` writes `bind-group`'s slot-local
; `entry`, which shadows the *global* `entry` — a lowerable sugar form. The
; local body is never a hook, so nothing lowers. Before the worklist resolved
; local-first it looked `entry` up globally, fired `test/identity-v1` on the
; local node, and emitted an `(entry-normal)` missing its required `:must` —
; see the sibling `lowering-global-sugar-at-root-lowers` for that shape where
; it is intended.
(plugin :name p :version "1.0.0"
  (form :name entry :open true
    :lowering (lowering :hook test/identity-v1 :produces [entry-normal]))
  (form :name entry-normal
    (key :name must :type number :optional false))
  (form :name bind-group
    (form :name entry)))

(bind-group (entry))
